  },
  "body": "`TopologyTestDriver` shares an offset counter between concrete topics matching the same source pattern. After records A, A, B, it assigns offsets 0, 1, 2 instead of 0, 1, 0. This can make a position-bound store query succeed before the required record from B has been processed.\n\nTrack regular input offsets per concrete topic, with separate counters for global inputs. The change is limited to test-driver offset generation: pattern inputs retain their existing task queues, assignment, and idling behavior. Mock commit offsets derived from input records change with the corrected metadata; the synthetic queue/commit model is retained.\n\nAdd regression coverage for per-topic record metadata and position-bound queries in `at_least_once` and `exactly_once_v2` modes.\n\n",
